e living temporarily with the claimant  ","tree_line_end":750,"tree_line_start":745},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Foster children  ","tree_line_end":756,"tree_line_start":751},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28377 The DM should fully disregard payments\n1\n made by or on behalf of ","tree_line_end":766,"tree_line_start":757},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.  a LA under its duty to provide  ","tree_line_end":772,"tree_line_start":767},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.1  accommodation and  ","tree_line_end":778,"tree_line_start":773},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.2 maintenance  ","tree_line_end":785,"tree_line_start":779},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"for a child it is looking after (including under Continuing Care arranegments)\n2\n or  ","tree_line_end":794,"tree_line_start":786},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2.  a voluntary organization under certain legislation\n3\n or  ","tree_line_end":805,"tree_line_start":795},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"3.  a LA\n4\n  ","tree_line_end":814,"tree_line_start":806},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" for children who are living with claimants under fostering arrangements.  ","tree_line_end":820,"tree_line_start":815},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" Note: These allowances should not be treated as earnings.  ","tree_line_end":826,"tree_line_start":821},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 27; IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 26; 2 Children Act 1989, s 23(2)(a); Children (Scotland) Act 1995, s 26 or 26A; 3 Children Act 1989, s 59(1)(a); 4 Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009, regs 33 or 51 ","tree_line_end":832,"tree_line_start":827},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Kinship care ","tree_line_end":838,"tree_line_start":833},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28378 In Scotland an LA may place a child with another person in an arrangement often referred to “Kinship care”\n1\n. Any payment made by the LA to the person providing care should be fully disregarded\n2\n. ","tree_line_end":852,"tree_line_start":839},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009, reg 10; 2 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 27; IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 26 ","tree_line_end":858,"tree_line_start":853},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Payments for the welfare of children  ","tree_line_end":864,"tree_line_start":859},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28379 Certain legislation\n1\n concerning the welfare of children applies in England, Wales and Scotland\n2\n. This applies to certain children who were being looked after by a LA. ","tree_line_end":878,"tree_line_start":865},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 CLC Act 2000; Children (Leaving Care) SS Benefit Regs, reg 1(1);  2 Children (Leaving Care) SS Benefits (Scotland) Regs, reg 1 ","tree_line_end":884,"tree_line_start":879},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28380  The DM should fully disregard payments made by LAs under child-care law\n1 ","tree_line_end":893,"tree_line_start":885},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.  to promote the welfare of children and ","tree_line_end":899,"tree_line_start":894},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2.  to prevent people being taken into care  ","tree_line_end":905,"tree_line_start":900},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" unless the claimant or a member of the family is involved in a TD\n2\n.  ","tree_line_end":915,"tree_line_start":906},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 Children (Leaving Care) Act 2000 (Comm No. 2 & Cons Prov) Order, Sch 1, para (c) & Sch 4, para (c); Children Act 1989, s 17, 23B, 23C or 24A; SW (Scot) Act 68, s 12; Children (Scotland) Act 1995, s 22, 26A, 29 or 30; 2 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 29(1); IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 28(1) ","tree_line_end":921,"tree_line_start":916},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28381 Where ","tree_line_end":926,"tree_line_start":922},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1. a former child (aged over 18) who was in the claimant’s care still lives with the claimant and ","tree_line_end":933,"tree_line_start":927},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2. the LA makes payments under certain child care law\n1\n to the former child in care and ","tree_line_end":942,"tree_line_start":934},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"3. the former child in care passes the payments on to the claimant ","tree_line_end":949,"tree_line_start":943},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" those payments received by the claimant are disregarded unless the claimant or a member of the family is involved in a TD\n2\n. ","tree_line_end":958,"tree_line_start":950},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 Children Act 89, s 23C; Children (Scotland) Act 95, s 22, 26A or 29; 2 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 29(2) & (5); IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 28(2) & (5) ","tree_line_end":964,"tree_line_start":959},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28382  The DM should take into account the income in full in DMG 28380 or DMG 28381 if  ","tree_line_end":970,"tree_line_start":965},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.  the claimant or  ","tree_line_end":974,"tree_line_start":971},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2.  a member of the family  ","tree_line_end":980,"tree_line_start":975},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" is involved in a TD\n1\n.  ","tree_line_end":990,"tree_line_start":981},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Note: These payments may be made to people who were in LA care.  ","tree_line_end":994,"tree_line_start":991},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 29(4); IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 28(4); JS Act 95, s 14;  SS CB Act 92, s 124(1), 126 & 127  ","tree_line_end":1000,"tree_line_start":995},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Payments for people temporarily in the claimant’s care  ","tree_line_end":1006,"tree_line_start":1001},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28383  The DM should fully disregard payments to a claimant or partner for a person who  ","tree_line_end":1012,"tree_line_start":1007},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.  is not normally a member of the claimant's household and  ","tree_line_end":1018,"tree_line_start":1013},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2.  is temporarily in the claimant's care\n1  ","tree_line_end":1026,"tree_line_start":1019},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":" when payments are made by a LA, HA, a voluntary organization, a clinical commissioning group, the NHS Commissioning Board, a Local Health Board or the person concerned under specified legislation\n2\n.  ","tree_line_end":1036,"tree_line_start":1027},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Note 1: This could include payments to a claimant under the Adult Placement or Shared Lives Scheme from a LA’s own resources. ","tree_line_end":1042,"tree_line_start":1037},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"Note 2: Payments made by a LA does not include payments of HB made in respect of the person concerned. ","tree_line_end":1048,"tree_line_start":1043},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 JSA Regs, Sch 7, para 28; IS (Gen) Regs, Sch 9, para 27; 2 NA Act 48, s 26(3A) ","tree_line_end":1054,"tree_line_start":1049},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"28384  This type of payment is often made to people providing “respite care”. This is short-term care provided to give a disabled person's usual carer a break from their caring responsibilities. People providing respite care should not be treated as  ","tree_line_end":1060,"tree_line_start":1055},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1.  engaged in remunerative work or  ","tree_line_end":1067,"tree_line_start":1061},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"2.  receiving earnings from S/E\n1\n.  ","tree_line_end":1078,"tree_line_start":1068},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"1 JSA Regs, reg 100(2)(b); IS (Gen) Regs, reg 37(2)(b)  ","tree_line_end":1082,"tree_line_start":1079},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1089,"tree_line_start":1083},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1094,"tree_line_start":1090},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1099,"tree_line_start":1095},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1105,"tree_line_start":1100},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1111,"tree_line_start":1106},{"depth":1,"role":"P","text":"","tree_line_end":1117,"tree_line_start":1112},{"depth":1,"rol